86 0 obj
<</K 47/P 102 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/S/H5/T(These findings contradict theories linking loneliness to aggression or extremism. Loneliness instead appears connected to political withdrawal and lower willingness to engage in risky activism. Younger adults higher support for political violence likely \
stems from political distrust, social frustration, and digital-era socialization„not loneliness. Loneliness does not drive support for political violence. Age is the strongest predictor of political violence attitudes. Future research should distinguish l\
oneliness from online isolation and explore whether ideological extremity moderates the relationship between psychosocial distress and political aggression.)>>
endobj
